 camacho:{name:'Casa Camacho & Malasaña',area:'Malasaña',lat:40.4265,lng:-3.7037,address:'Calle de San Andrés 4',wiki:W('Malasaña'),wikiLabel:'Wikipedia · neighbourhood',story:'A compact, traditional tavern in a neighbourhood associated with the Movida and late-night Madrid. Have a vermouth or try the house’s well-known yayo if you fancy it.',secret:'The fun is in the mix: traditional bar habits and a neighbourhood that keeps reinventing itself.',practical:'Saturday published closing 02:00. Standing and crowds are part of the likely experience; keep the next stop flexible.',source:SOURCES.camacho,kind:'night'},
 trash:{name:'The flock takes the city',area:'Plaza de la Villa',lat:40.4153,lng:-3.7108,address:'Plaza de la Villa · Calle Mayor approaches',wiki:W('Transhumance'),wikiLabel:'Wikipedia · transhumance',story:'Seasonal herding comes into the city for a modern celebration of historic livestock routes. The Madrid festival began in 1994; the symbolic payment recalls an agreement from 1418.',secret:'This is living countryside arriving in the capital, not an uninterrupted medieval parade.',practical:'Sunday 25 Oct: reach the area 10:30–10:45. The city estimates the flock at Villa around 11:15–11:25. No Sol or Cibeles this year. Times are approximate.',source:SOURCES.trash,kind:'event'},
 rastro:{mapQuery:'Plaza de Cascorro',name:'El Rastro',area:'La Latina',lat:40.4096,lng:-3.7075,address:'Cascorro & Ribera de Curtidores',wiki:W('El Rastro'),story:'The Sunday flea market: browse the main slope, then take a few side streets. Old objects, odd finds and people-watching make this a good place to wander without a shopping list.',secret:'Set a tiny challenge: find the most inexplicable object of the morning. Buying it is entirely optional.',practical:'Sunday 09:00–15:00. Aim for roughly 12:15–14:00 after the flock. Allow for temporary crowd controls and blocked crossings.',source:SOURCES.rastro,kind:'market'},
